Nina (AE): heads-up — NovaPay POC is blocked. They get a JSON.parse error in their function-calling flow when streaming=true: "Unexpected token } in JSON at position 482". They need a quick workaround.

Diego (SE): which model + SDK? can you paste the raw assembled stream? any 429s in ingress?

Nina (AE): model rdx-medium-2026, SDK 0.10.1 (js). Streaming=true. they concat chunks and then JSON.parse. Raw assembled stream they captured: 

```
{"role":"assistant","content":{"tool_call":{"name":"create_payment","args":"{\"amount\":100,\"currency\":\"USD\"}"}}}
}}partial_tail
```

Diego (SE): looks like extra trailing bytes after the JSON object. two possibilities: (1) model emitted a small progress suffix after the final object; (2) a 429/connection reset dropped the last bytes and client appended something. can you repro with streaming=false?

Nina (AE): streaming=false works (but customer dislikes latency). repro with smaller prompt doesn't fail. this seems load-dependent.

Lena (eng): probable: when tool routing + streaming, we occasionally emit small telemetry/progress tokens post-object. additionally, if the stream is interrupted (429 or connection cut), clients sometimes stash incomplete buffers and append markers. short term: advise the customer to sanitize the assembled buffer before JSON.parse. example quick sanitizer (JS):

```js
function sanitizeToFirstObject(buf) {
  // crude but effective: find first balanced JSON object
  let depth = 0;
  let start = buf.indexOf('{');
  if (start === -1) throw new Error('no json');
  for (let i = start; i < buf.length; i++) {
    if (buf[i] === '{') depth++;
    else if (buf[i] === '}') depth--;
    if (depth === 0) return buf.slice(start, i + 1);
  }
  throw new Error('incomplete json');
}

const sanitized = sanitizeToFirstObject(assembled);
const parsed = JSON.parse(sanitized);
```

Lena (eng): long-term: I'll add a sanitizeStreamingJson option to the JS SDK that runs this logic when json_mode=STRICT and streaming=true. Will target v0.10.2 patch and publish tonight.

